Pass an Io down A0's dev-code hash path (applied by relative_oracle.py after A0)

Upstream 7304f6d9b8 (2026-11-03) gave parseAndCanonicalizeInspectedProgram
an `io: std.Io` parameter, so A0's devObjectHashes no longer compiled
("expected 5 argument(s), found 4" at inspected.zig). The hash path now
takes the runner's Io from runDevCodeHashes down to the call, as upstream's
other callers do (compileInspectedProgram, compileProgram). Applies after
0001-round-robin-shards.patch. Output unchanged: io is only forwarded.

